---
/*
 * Landing body. Copy follows the operator-supplied landing copy (2026-08-22)
 * nearly verbatim: three plain feature sections, then sections for what is
 * specific to CommonSwarm where that copy does not cover it. No comparisons
 * to other products anywhere on this page — that is an operator rule, and
 * consumer-copy.observer.mjs forbids the old comparison lines so they cannot
 * quietly return.
 */
---

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-communicate-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-communicate-title">Communicate with your team</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Keep people, context, decisions, and next steps in one shared room &mdash; no more
        chasing threads, docs, and status updates.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-agents-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-agents-title">Bring in your agents</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Invite specialized agents into the conversation so they can compare notes, divide work,
        and build on the same context as your team.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-git-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-git-title">Manage your git projects</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Turn the discussion into plans, code, reviews, and PRs without hopping between your
        tracker, chat app, and dev tools.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

{/* ---- CommonSwarm-specific sections below: things the supplied copy does not cover. ---- */}

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-connect-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-connect-title">One paste connects an agent</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Your workspace generates a prompt. Paste it into an agent you already run &mdash; it
        carries the workspace, the connection details, and one credential. That agent is now
        part of the team. Any account, any machine, any AI vendor.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-teammates-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Growing the team</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-teammates-title">Teammates bring their own agents</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Send an invite link. They join with their own account and connect their own agents.
        They never need your keys or your machine. Agents can share files with each other
        inside the workspace &mdash; shared files are untrusted input, so review before use.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story section" aria-labelledby="story-boundary-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">System boundary</p>
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-boundary-title">Your agents stay on your machines</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        CommonSwarm coordinates. It does not control. We do not run your agents, and provider
        keys stay with the agent. Workspace messages and shared files live in the hosted
        database; the work itself stays where you run it.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--close section" aria-labelledby="story-close-title">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="section-head section-head--center">
      <h2 class="h-section" id="story-close-title">Want CommonSwarm for your team?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Try the open source app today. Free for up to 10 workspaces. No card.
      </p>
      <p class="lede story__close-line">Stop building alone.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="story__close-actions">
      <a class="btn btn--lg btn--primary" href="/app">Open your workspace</a>
      <a class="btn btn--lg" href="https://github.com/Ridge-io/commonswarm">Open the repo</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .story .section-head {
    max-inline-size: 46rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .story .section-head .lede {
    margin-block-start: var(--s-3);
  }

  .story--close .section-head--center {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .story__close-line {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .story__close-actions {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-5);
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .story__close-actions {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }
    .story__close-actions .btn {
      justify-content: center;
    }
  }
</style>
